{
  "wireMagic": "pb3",
  "pens": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wsWinStyles": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wpWinPositions": [ {
  
  } ],
  "events": [ {
    "tStartMs": 2730,
    "dDurationMs": 4580,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The basic laws of physics – things like\nF=ma, “gravity is inversely proportional"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 7310,
    "dDurationMs": 3910,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to the distance squared”, Schrodinger’s\nequation, and so on – don’t say anything"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 11220,
    "dDurationMs": 1940,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "about the direction of time."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 13160,
    "dDurationMs": 4390,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Sure, they relate what’s going on now to\nwhat happens next, and to what happened previously,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 17550,
    "dDurationMs": 3860,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but there’s no distinction between forwards\nand backwards in time."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 21410,
    "dDurationMs": 4199,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The past and future are on an equal footing,\nas far as the microscopic laws of physics"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 25609,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "are concerned."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 26609,
    "dDurationMs": 3991,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In the macroscopic world, however, there is\none rule that does have time going in one"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 30600,
    "dDurationMs": 2900,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "direction only: the second law of thermodynamics."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 33500,
    "dDurationMs": 4780,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That says that any isolated system will tend\ntowards increasing entropy, or disorder."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 38280,
    "dDurationMs": 4640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Like how cold milk and hot coffee mix together\ninto luke-warm coffee-milk, but will never"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 42920,
    "dDurationMs": 1729,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "“unmix”."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 44649,
    "dDurationMs": 4061,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Once a system gets to its fully-disordered\nstate -- its equilibrium -- there’s no more"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 48710,
    "dDurationMs": 3390,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "direction of increasing entropy to determine\nthe arrow of time."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 52100,
    "dDurationMs": 4790,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So the fact that we experience the flow of\ntime right now means that we’re not in equilibrium."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 56890,
    "dDurationMs": 2099,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "There are basically two ways that could happen."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 58989,
    "dDurationMs": 5691,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Either the universe just happens to be, right\nnow, in this particular, low-entropy, configuration"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 64680,
    "dDurationMs": 5220,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "with two directions of time flowing out forward\nand backward from it with increasing entropy"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 69900,
    "dDurationMs": 5070,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in both directions; or at some point in the\nfar distant past the universe started with"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 74970,
    "dDurationMs": 3520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "even lower entropy, and disorder has been\nincreasing ever since."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 78490,
    "dDurationMs": 2630,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "[Spoiler alert: it’s option number two.]"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 81120,
    "dDurationMs": 3090,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That low-entropy configuration was the Big\nBang."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 84210,
    "dDurationMs": 5540,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "13.8 billion years ago, the universe was hot,\ndense, smooth, and rapidly expanding."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 89750,
    "dDurationMs": 4420,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "A smooth dense plasma of particles might not\nseem organized \u0026 low-entropy, but when the"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 94170,
    "dDurationMs": 5110,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "density of matter is extremely high, the gravitational\nforce between particles is enormous."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 99280,
    "dDurationMs": 4290,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Smoothness, in the face of such tendencies,\nis not equilibrium, but is actually a very"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 103570,
    "dDurationMs": 2630,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "delicately-balanced, low entropy state."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 106200,
    "dDurationMs": 4720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Things want to be gravitationally clumped\ntogether into concentrated configurations"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 110920,
    "dDurationMs": 3270,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "like proto-stars, proto-galaxies, or even\nblack holes."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 114190,
    "dDurationMs": 3620,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "What would a high-entropy, equilibrium universe\nlook like?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 117810,
    "dDurationMs": 1570,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It would be empty space."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 119380,
    "dDurationMs": 4160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And indeed, that’s where we’re headed:\nthe universe is expanding and diluting, and"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 123540,
    "dDurationMs": 3710,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "eventually all the stars will burn out and\nblack holes will evaporate and we’ll be"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 127250,
    "dDurationMs": 2780,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "left with nothing but emptiness in every direction."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 130030,
    "dDurationMs": 4400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "At that point, time’s arrow will have disappeared,\nand nothing like life or consciousness will"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 134430,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "be possible."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 135430,
    "dDurationMs": 5050,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The fact that our sky is decorated with billions\nof stars and galaxies, and our biosphere is"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 140480,
    "dDurationMs": 4119,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "teeming with life, is a reflection of our\nlow-entropy beginnings."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 144599,
    "dDurationMs": 3901,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "We don’t know why the universe started in\nsuch an orderly initial state, but we should"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 148500,
    "dDurationMs": 4129,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "be glad it did: it gave us the non-equilibrium\nstarting point that’s necessary for the"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 152629,
    "dDurationMs": 2801,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "flow of time, as we know it, to exist."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 155430,
    "dDurationMs": 3839,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Everything that followed -- from the formation\nof stars and galaxies to the origin of life"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 159269,
    "dDurationMs": 2470,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "-- has been a story of increasing entropy."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 161739,
    "dDurationMs": 4631,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Time’s arrow isn’t a deep feature of the\nmost fundamental laws of physics; it owes"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 166370,
    "dDurationMs": 5899,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "its existence to the specific initial conditions\nof our universe."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 172269,
    "dDurationMs": 3590,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Hey, Henry here, thanks for watching."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 175859,
    "dDurationMs": 3011,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This is the first [second, third, etc] video\nin a series about time and entropy made in"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 178870,
    "dDurationMs": 2110,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "collaboration with physicist Sean Carroll."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 180980,
    "dDurationMs": 3640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The series is supported with funding from\nGoogle’s Making and Science initiative,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 184620,
    "dDurationMs": 3629,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which seeks to encourage more young people\n(and people of all ages) to learn about and"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 188249,
    "dDurationMs": 3940,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "fall in love with science and the world around\nthem, and the videos are based off of Sean’s"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 192189,
    "dDurationMs": 3720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "book “The Big Picture: On the Origins of\nLife, Meaning, and the Universe Itself,”"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 195909,
    "dDurationMs": 4690,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which you can find online or in bookstores\naround the world."
    } ]
  } ]
}
